<title>SWEDEN: ABB BUYS POLISH SWITCHGEAR CO.</title>
<headline>ABB BUYS POLISH SWITCHGEAR CO.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-08-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swiss/Swedish engineering group ABB said on Tuesday it had signed agreements with the Polish government to acquire 80 percent of the ZWAR group, one of Poland's leading switchgear and high-voltage equipment makers.  </p>
<p>The Polish government will retain a 20 percent stake of the company, to be renamed ABB ZWAR, ABB said in a statement.</p>
<p>The ZWAR group has four factories, two in Warsaw, one north of Warsaw in Przasnysz, and one west of Gdansk in Lebork.</p>
<p>In total it employs 1,750 people and is a major supplier to the Polish market.</p>
<p>The purchase remains subject to approval by regulatory authorities.</p>
<p>ABB said including this acquisition, it now employs 8,500 people in Poland.</p>
<p>-- Belinda Goldsmith, Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1045</p>
